WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.020
Welcome back to Things You Missed, and prepare
yourself to relive your childhood nightmares

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:08.530
because in today’s episode we’re looking
at the teasers for Scary Stories To Tell In

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:09.530
The Dark.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:12.139
Stick around to the end of this video if you
want to hear how these classic stories tie

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.950
together in the new movie.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.960
At the time of making this video there are
four teasers for Scary Stories To Tell In

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:26.250
The Dark and they are filled with references
to the original trilogy of children’s horror

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.250
stories.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.920
I was more of a Scary Stories for Sleepovers
kind of kid myself, maybe a little Goosebumps,

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:33.800
but I’m definitely interested in the new
movie because the teasers look intense, like

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.860
they’re aimed for kids who grew up with
these stories and are now adults.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.320
Let’s take a look at the first clip.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.200
"Based on the iconic book series.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:47.700
Scary stories."

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:51.190
The creature in this teaser is a recreation
of the monster from short story called The

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.579
Dream which appeared in Scary Stories 3.

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:57.630
The tale is about an artist named Lucy who
goes from town to town to paint various villages.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:01.540
She decides to go to a village called Kingston,
but the night before leaving, she has a dream

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.930
about this pale skinned woman in warning her
to flee while she can, that this is an evil

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:06.930
place.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:10.330
So the next morning, she wakes up and decides
to go to a different town, Dorset.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:13.560
As she’s looking for a place to stay in
Dorset, looks at a room that resembles the

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.070
room from her dream, which makes her uneasy.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:19.920
The landlady goes to make some tea and give
Lucy time to think it over, when the pale

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.549
skinned woman appears before her, sending
Lucy running for the hills.

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:27.119
In the movie, the creature approaches a boy
down a long hall with a red light, which tells

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:31.119
us that the movie may not just be an anthology
of scary stories adapted into short films,

00:01:31.119 --> 00:01:34.920
but rather that the stories exist as stories
within the world of the movie, and maybe the

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.530
characters find themselves in trouble when
they discover that these stories are true.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:41.020
Another story from the book is showcased in
the next teaser.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:48.440
"Scary stories."

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:51.720
The story is called The Red Spot, and it’s
about a girl named Ruth whose face is paid

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.750
a visit by a spider as she sleeps.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:57.171
The next morning she notices a red spot on
her cheek that looks like a spider bite, but

00:01:57.171 --> 00:02:01.390
instead of going away over time, the spot
grows until one day, it bursts while she’s

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:05.590
in the bath, and tons of baby spiders come
crawling out because the boil was actually

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:07.479
filled with spider eggs.

00:02:07.479 --> 00:02:11.640
In the movie, the girl discovers a spider’s
leg in the red spot before it bursts.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.230
And she’s in high school when it happens.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:16.920
The roof tiles are similar to those in the
first teaser, leading me to believe they could

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.600
all be in this school together.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.840
If you know anything about the Scary Stories
books, you probably recognized the next monster.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:29.660
"Who... took... my... big... toe?"

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:35.360
This is the first story in the first book,
in which a boy pulls out this toe from the

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:40.489
woods, and he brings it home and for some
reason his Mom prepares as part of her soup…

00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:42.590
and they eat it for dinner.

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:45.750
If you never want to have soup again, I completely
understand.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:48.520
But not much is different here in the movie,
because the next thing that happens is the

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.160
monster then comes after the boy.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:54.080
The monster in the book is also described
as having a huge mouth and teeth to chomp

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.940
it’s victims’ bones, but the movie version
looks more like The Green Giant.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:02.069
The last teaser is a little bit more ambiguous,
it has the boy from the first teaser, who

00:03:02.069 --> 00:03:04.990
keeps saying, “we’re next”, and then
this other kid is attacked by the Green Goblin

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:05.990
looking-ghoulo.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:09.239
I don’t think there’s a specific story
or piece of artwork that this guy is from

00:03:09.239 --> 00:03:13.410
in the books, so my guess is that this is
one of the many unseen monsters from the stories.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:17.450
Probably 30% of all these stories in those
books follow the exact same formula where

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:20.830
someone’s in a spooky house or location,
and they hear something coming towards them

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:24.400
and getting closer and closer and then whatever
it is that’s making the sound disappears

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.400
and the story ends.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:29.330
So my guess is that this friendly looking
guy is one of those monsters, but this time

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:30.790
he comes and breaks down the door.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:34.590
There’s also this other shot in the teaser,
this last one is just packed with stuff, and

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:36.640
it appears to be water dripping into a horse
trough.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:40.409
There are three stories with horses in the
series, one where a witch turns a man into

00:03:40.409 --> 00:03:44.841
a horse at night, one where two kids are attacked
by a ghostly tribe of men on horseback, and

00:03:44.841 --> 00:03:48.491
one where a fortune teller predicts that a
man’s horse will lead to his death, which

00:03:48.491 --> 00:03:50.450
is most likely what we’re seeing here.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:53.320
So how are all of these stories going to connect
to make a movie?

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:57.190
According to the studio, a group of teenagers
in the 60s discovers a book of stories whose

00:03:57.190 --> 00:04:01.370
legends begin to turn real, resulting in horrific
deaths across their town.

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:04.540
So I think they’ll discover that the tales
of horror read about in the books are the

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:06.870
key to overcoming these monsters in real life.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:10.769
Let me know in the comments if there are any
stories you’d like to see incorporated in

00:04:10.769 --> 00:04:14.970
the movie, and remember to subscribe to CZsWorld
and ring the deathbell for notifications,

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:18.760
so you don’t miss out on upcoming Things
You Missed episodes like the Scary Stories

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:20.079
Official Trailer.

00:04:20.079 --> 00:04:23.231
And if you love short horror stories click
the playlist on the left to listen to some

00:04:23.231 --> 00:04:24.789
creepy stories that I’ve written.

00:04:24.789 --> 00:04:27.070
As always, I will see you in the next one.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:29.080
Assuming we both survive.

